Somewhere past his hundred-and-twentieth year — late middle age by dwarven measure — Copperjaw still waddles out of his converted storage-container office to run [[Sableclutch Scrap]], letting the giant crusher near the front gate deter the unwelcome. The crude copper prosthetic where his bottom jaw ought to be gives him his name; the mashed nose and the accumulated wreckage suggest he was fighting long before he took up scrap, and has not stopped since. From that same container office he also crafted the contents of the [[metal suitcase]].
